    "q-74556": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74556",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & k-6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-15.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-15\\,⇒\\,k=15.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
