    "q-74594": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74594",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
